From 1216ff4766924026396adfc040ef3e7617743d80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Klemm <github@tklemm.eu>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:06:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build notification handle groups with each instead of
 Hash#map

Hash has no map of its own, so Fanout#build_handle went through
Enumerable#map, which iterates the Hash with an internal C block that
then calls the Ruby block for every group. Iterating with each and
pushing into a local Array calls the Ruby block directly: one object
less per instrumented event with active subscribers, and fewer
instructions.

The groups are built in the same order and passed to Handle the same way.
---
 activesupport/lib/active_support/notifications/fanout.rb | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/activesupport/lib/active_support/notifications/fanout.rb b/activesupport/lib/active_support/notifications/fanout.rb
index daa780e6ab..46883cdee2 100644
--- a/activesupport/lib/active_support/notifications/fanout.rb
+++ b/activesupport/lib/active_support/notifications/fanout.rb
@@ -374,8 +374,9 @@ def build_handle(name, id, payload)
         if groups.empty?
           NullHandle
         else
-          instances = groups.map do |group_klass, grouped_listeners|
-            group_klass.new(grouped_listeners, name, id, payload)
+          instances = []
+          groups.each do |group_klass, grouped_listeners|
+            instances << group_klass.new(grouped_listeners, name, id, payload)
           end
           Handle.new(name, id, instances, payload)
         end
